    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d487">

                <pb facs="0670" n="576" sameAs="frus:frus1896/pg576"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Olney to Mr.
                            Bayard.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1896-02-13"><hi rendition="#italic">February 13,
                        1896</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 993.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have to inform you that your dispatch No.
                    590, of the 31st ultimo, stating that you had learned from the British foreign
                    office that Mr. Knight, the United States vice-consul at Cape Town, had arrived
                    at Pretoria, and that he is making arrangements there for the defense of
                    American citizens, has been received.</p>
                <p>You are correct in your inference that this Government is now in direct
                    communication with its agents in the Transvaal.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Richard Olney.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
